{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/535920-biting-off-more-than-you-can-chew","id":535920,"title":"Biting off more than you can chew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-01T14:16:12-07:00","id":535920,"title":"Biting off more than you can chew","content":"Let's face it; although most players/storytellers enjoy Hunter for the &quot;humanity, hell yeah!&quot; motif it can be played for, the canonical truth of it is that it is very much a horror game, and a big part of the horror is that humans are really outgunned by what's out there. Yes, the Vigil is eternal, but the hunters are not, and while hunters can win, mistakes are very unforgiving, and some &quot;prey&quot; is more than capable of turning the tables without much effort.<br /> <br /> I got to thinking about this fact after reading one of my older posts, where I noted that if were playing a Mage captured by the MM, I would gladly spam the biggest, nastiest spells I could think of, because I'm in a lose-lose situation; getting wiped from existence by Paradox - but hopefully not before calling up an Abyssal monster that will make things very unpleasant for my captors when they stumble into it - is less painful than being tortured to death &quot;for the sake of my soul&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm just curious to know if anyone has ever made use of this fact in their games, or seen it used by other Storytellers? Could be build-up to your own sessions - finding the remains/hearing through the grapevine/investigating the disappearances/etc of hunters who bit off more then they could chew - or could just be the fallout from your missions going wrong, or whatever. I'd like to hear the stories of hunters being reminded that they are, at best, on equal terms to the creatures of the night - NOT their superiors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}